    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI've got the following keymap for MiniPick:\r\n```\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>f', function()\r\n    MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\r\n    window = { config = { width = vim.o.columns } },\r\n    })\r\nend, { remap = false, silent = true, desc = '[F]ind in files via ripgrep' })\r\n```\r\nWhen I try it in my `.config/nvim` folder and type `callback` I get all the expected results:\r\n<img width=\"963\" height=\"1286\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-09 at 7 32 58 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc61fea0-e1d5-4dd4-958f-eae80d4f6927\" />\r\n\r\nWhen I prefix it with a `'` character like the docs say should indicate a non-fuzzy search, I get nothing:\r\n<img width=\"913\" height=\"1287\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-09 at 7 32 17 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e82164ec-1282-4c3a-864b-eca4580bdc85\" />\r\n\r\nI've got to be missing something obvious here",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've got the following keymap for MiniPick:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;f', function()\n    MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\n    window = { config = { width = vim.o.columns } },\n    })\nend, { remap = false, silent = true, desc = '[F]ind in files via ripgrep' })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;leader&gt;f', function()\n    MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\n    window = { config = { width = vim.o.columns } },\n    })\nend, { remap = false, silent = true, desc = '[F]ind in files via ripgrep' })\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I try it in my <code class=\"notranslate\">.config/nvim</code> folder and type <code class=\"notranslate\">callback</code> I get all the expected results:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/13407106/487830515-fc61fea0-e1d5-4dd4-958f-eae80d4f6927.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..JI9EiPERQWXs47rfXu5ns47UjtCp97UVoMfMmotB2EM\"><img width=\"963\" height=\"1286\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-09 at 7 32 58 AM\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/13407106/487830515-fc61fea0-e1d5-4dd4-958f-eae80d4f6927.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..JI9EiPERQWXs47rfXu5ns47UjtCp97UVoMfMmotB2EM\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1286px;; aspect-ratio: 963 / 1286; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I prefix it with a <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> character like the docs say should indicate a non-fuzzy search, I get nothing:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/13407106/487830605-e82164ec-1282-4c3a-864b-eca4580bdc85.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..zIMdsavAAlEomMd7-RCixJjtgtfgMQWzgg2xviyLBn4\"><img width=\"913\" height=\"1287\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-09 at 7 32 17 AM\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/13407106/487830605-e82164ec-1282-4c3a-864b-eca4580bdc85.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..zIMdsavAAlEomMd7-RCixJjtgtfgMQWzgg2xviyLBn4\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1287px;; aspect-ratio: 913 / 1287; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've got to be missing something obvious here</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nI've got the following keymap for MiniPick:\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>f', function()\n    MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\n    window = { config = { width = vim.o.columns } },\n    })\nend, { remap = false, silent = true, desc = '[F]ind in files via ripgrep' })\n\nWhen I try it in my .config/nvim folder and type callback I get all the expected results:\n\nWhen I prefix it with a ' character like the docs say should indicate a non-fuzzy search, I get nothing:\n\nI've got to be missing something obvious here",
