    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Prepending query with `'` results in the exact match only [when matching is done with `default_match()`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6bf9eccaf2a5395b254bc031f9812cf163ca4187/doc/mini-pick.txt#L188-L189). That is usually the case for pickers *except* `grep_live` which [treats query/prompt directly as pattern](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6bf9eccaf2a5395b254bc031f9812cf163ca4187/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1132) to match using CLI tool (`rg` by default). So typing `callback` in prompt in this case already matches it non-fuzzy. If prepended with `'`, it tries to match pattern `'callback`, which it can not.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Prepending query with <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code> results in the exact match only <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6bf9eccaf2a5395b254bc031f9812cf163ca4187/doc/mini-pick.txt#L188-L189\">when matching is done with <code class=\"notranslate\">default_match()</code></a>. That is usually the case for pickers <em>except</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">grep_live</code> which <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/6bf9eccaf2a5395b254bc031f9812cf163ca4187/doc/mini-pick.txt#L1132\">treats query/prompt directly as pattern</a> to match using CLI tool (<code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> by default). So typing <code class=\"notranslate\">callback</code> in prompt in this case already matches it non-fuzzy. If prepended with <code class=\"notranslate\">'</code>, it tries to match pattern <code class=\"notranslate\">'callback</code>, which it can not.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Prepending query with ' results in the exact match only when matching is done with default_match(). That is usually the case for pickers except grep_live which treats query/prompt directly as pattern to match using CLI tool (rg by default). So typing callback in prompt in this case already matches it non-fuzzy. If prepended with ', it tries to match pattern 'callback, which it can not.",
